  "body": "Analytics and request-log storage fixes for the request log. Every number below\nwas measured, and the ones that turned out to be measurement artifacts are\ncalled out rather than quietly dropped.\n\n## What was wrong\n\n1. **All 8 analytics endpoints blocked the event loop.** They are `async def`\n   calling synchronous SQLite inline. FastAPI only offloads plain `def`\n   handlers, so a slow aggregate stalled *every* concurrent request, including\n   `/health` and proxy traffic.\n2. **Connections were never closed.** `sqlite3.Connection.__exit__` only\n   commits or rolls back. Connections are GC-tracked rather than\n   reference-counted, so `with self._connect() as conn:` leaked file\n   descriptors until the next collection — measured 1 → 61 live connections\n   across 60 reads with GC disabled. This fired on the background writer's\n   flush path too, so it happened on ordinary proxy traffic, not just when the\n   dashboard was open.\n3. **Bodies were capped at flush, not at enqueue.** Queued records held\n   uncapped `input_text`, so a backlog could retain far more than the persisted\n   50k-char per-row limit.\n4. **The database file could only grow.** No `auto_vacuum`, so `prune()` freed\n   pages onto the freelist and never returned them to the filesystem.\n5. **Aggregates read the bodies they never referenced.** SQLite stores all\n   columns of a row together, so each of `stats()`'s seven scans walked\n   overflow pages holding up to 100k characters of text per row.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `request_log`: a closing `_connection()` helper used on every read and\n  maintenance path; the writer thread keeps one persistent connection instead\n  of reconnecting per batch.\n- `request_log`: cap bodies in `enqueue()` rather than at flush.\n- `request_log`: `auto_vacuum=INCREMENTAL` plus `incremental_vacuum` after a\n  prune that removed rows.\n- `request_log`: `idx_requests_stats`, covering the columns the aggregates read\n  so they run index-only.\n- `request_log`: list queries project explicit metadata columns with SQL-side\n  `substr` previews instead of `SELECT *`; `stats()` memoized for 5s.\n- `admin_routes`, `admin_websearch_routes`: all 8 endpoints run their SQLite\n  work via `asyncio.to_thread`.\n\nBoth migrations run on the writer thread. An earlier revision of this branch put\nthe conversion VACUUM in `RequestLogStore.__init__`, which is reached lazily from\na request handler — benchmarking caught construction regressing from 8 ms to\n17,304 ms, i.e. trading a ~3 s stall for a 17 s one. That is fixed and covered by\na test asserting construction stays under a second on a database still needing\nconversion.\n\n## Measured\n\nLive install, WSL/ext4, 4,946 rows / 149.5 MB. A/B by dropping and restoring the\nindex on a copy, unique filters per call to defeat the stats cache:\n\n| uncached | without index | with index |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `stats()` unfiltered | 242.6 ms | **23.1 ms** |\n| `stats(q=...)` | ~2.2-3.2 s | ~2.2-3.2 s |\n\n`stats(q=...)` is unchanged by design: a leading-wildcard `%LIKE%` over the body\ncolumns cannot use any index. That needs FTS5 and is deliberately out of scope.\n\nEvent-loop starvation, on the running server — 6 concurrent uncached queries at\n2.2-2.6 s each (all HTTP 200, full payloads):\n\n| | result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/health` probes completed | 80 / 80 |\n| probes over 500 ms | 0 |\n| worst `/health` latency | 18 ms |\n\nConnection hygiene: 1 → 61 live connections across 60 reads with GC disabled\nbecomes 3 → 3. Process footprint flat across 75 s idle after load (RSS, fds and\nthread count unchanged).\n\n### Correction to earlier figures\n\nInitial benchmarks ran against copies on NTFS and overstated the absolute\nnumbers by roughly 10x for the unfiltered case — the real ext4 baseline is\n~240 ms, not ~2,415 ms. The relative win is 10.5x, not 45x. The multi-second\nfigures are real only for the `q=`-filtered shape.\n\n### Costs\n\n- Threads 10 → 16 (`asyncio.to_thread` grows the default executor).\n- A one-time conversion VACUUM on an existing large log takes ~8-14 s on the\n  writer thread, and is logged.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdds regression tests for cap-before-enqueue, connection closure under disabled\nGC, eventual `auto_vacuum` mode, the covering index appearing in\n`EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN`, file size across insert/prune cycles, non-blocking\nconstruction, and stats cache behaviour. No new perf harness — these are cheap\ndeterministic assertions that run on every `uv run pytest`.\n\n`./scripts/ci.sh`: ruff format, ruff check and ty clean; 2,995 passed. 14\nfailures are pre-existing on `main` and unrelated — verified by running the same\ntests on a clean `main` checkout. Eight are websearch tests reading the\ndeveloper's real `~/.fcc/.env`; six are PowerShell installer wheel-checksum\ntests.\n\nVersion bumped 4.13.0 -> 4.13.1 (PATCH: fixes and refactors, no new config\nsurface) with `uv.lock` regenerated.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
