    "message": "fix(request-log): run the auto-vacuum conversion off the request path\n\nBenchmarking the previous commit against a copy of the live 148 MB request\ndatabase showed store construction regressing from 8 ms to 17,304 ms: the\none-time conversion VACUUM ran inside `RequestLogStore.__init__`, which is\nreached lazily from a request handler. That traded a 3s analytics stall for a\n17s one.\n\nThe conversion now runs on the writer thread instead, and logs how long it\ntook. A fresh database still adopts `auto_vacuum=INCREMENTAL` during init,\napplied outside the implicit transaction so the pragma actually persists and no\nconversion is needed at all.\n\nMeasured on a copy of the live database (4,882 rows / 147.8 MB):\n  construction        8 ms  ->     11 ms\n  stats() uncached  2415 ms  ->    828 ms (after background conversion)\n  list(q=...)        522 ms  ->    285 ms\n  live connections   1 -> 61  ->    3 -> 3 (60 reads, GC disabled)\n\nReplaces the immediate auto-vacuum assertion with one that polls for the\neventual mode, plus a test asserting construction stays under a second on a\ndatabase that still needs converting.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
