    "message": "perf(request-log): add a covering index so aggregates skip request bodies\n\nA peer review of the previous commit correctly pointed out that narrowing the\nlist projection buys little: `list_requests` was already ~8-13 ms because it is\nLIMIT 50 over an indexed sort. The real cost is `stats()`, which runs seven\naggregate scans, and SQLite stores every column of a row together — so each\nscan walks the overflow pages holding up to 100k characters of request and\nresponse text per row even though none of those aggregates reference the body\ncolumns.\n\nAdds `idx_requests_stats` covering the columns the aggregates actually read, so\nthey run index-only. Created on the writer thread alongside the auto-vacuum\nconversion, because building it on an existing large log takes seconds and must\nnot land on a request path.\n\nMeasured on a copy of the live database (4,882 rows / 147.8 MB):\n  stats() unfiltered   2415 ms -> 53.6 ms\n  list(limit=50)         12.8 ms -> 8.0 ms\n\n`stats(q=...)` stays ~2.3 s: the `%LIKE%` body filter has to read the text\ncolumns, so no index can cover it. That needs FTS5 and is deliberately out of\nscope here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
